		{
			"to": "western-civ/beethoven-ninth",
			"why": "The Eroica of 1804 began the long, personal symphony that Beethoven's Ninth, first heard in Vienna in 1824 when he was almost completely deaf, carried to its choral end."
		},
		{
			"to": "western-civ/french-revolution",
			"why": "Beethoven wrote the Eroica on Napoleon Bonaparte as First Consul, the general whose seizure of power in 1799 is where most historians end the Revolution, and scratched out his name when he made himself emperor."
		}
